c Pigeonhole principle: 2 pigeons, 1 hole
c This is UNSAT - can't fit 2 pigeons in 1 hole
c Variables: x_ij means pigeon i goes in hole j
c x1 = pigeon 1 in hole 1
c x2 = pigeon 2 in hole 1
c At least one pigeon in hole: (x1 OR x2)
c At most one pigeon per hole: (NOT x1 OR NOT x2)
c Each pigeon must be somewhere: (x1) AND (x2)
c Combined: UNSAT because both must be in hole 1 but only one can fit
p cnf 2 4
1 2 0
-1 -2 0
1 0
2 0
